{"uid":"e9290fd1d0c7f68b","name":"test_verdict_gate_run_iteration_call_site_passes_no_extra_context","fullName":"tests.test_peer_verdict_gate#test_verdict_gate_run_iteration_call_site_passes_no_extra_context","historyId":"4c508e36569240ee41b11bff1f4d0152","time":{"start":1791956536984,"stop":1791956536998,"duration":14},"description":"A narrower, unit-level pin of the same fact: with no operator ruling\n    recorded (the common case), `_step_verdict_gate` calls\n    `run_iteration('verdict_gate', ...)` with an EMPTY `extra` -- unlike\n    `_run_review_iteration`, which always passes\n    `extra=self._review_extra_context()`. Spies on the real\n    `LoopSupervisor.run_iteration` call rather than reading source, so a\n    future refactor that reintroduces review-shaped context would fail\n    this test even if it renamed the parameter.\n\n    Task 018 (D.8, #196): the one thing the call site does pass is the\n    operator-ruling context, which is `''` unless a ruling exists under the\n    `:ro` /config mount -- so `loop_mod.CONFIG_DIR` is pointed at an empty\n    scratch directory here to keep this pin independent of whatever the\n    host running the suite has mounted. The non-empty case (a wave-scoped\n    ruling reaching this exact call site after a replan) is covered by\n    tests/test_operator_ruling.py::\n    test_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A narrower, unit-level pin of the same fact: with no operator ruling<br />\nrecorded (the common case), <code>_step_verdict_gate</code> calls<br />\n<code>run_iteration('verdict_gate', ...)</code> with an EMPTY <code>extra</code> -- unlike<br />\n<code>_run_review_iteration</code>, which always passes<br />\n<code>extra=self._review_extra_context()</code>. Spies on the real<br />\n<code>LoopSupervisor.run_iteration</code> call rather than reading source, so a<br />\nfuture refactor that reintroduces review-shaped context would fail<br />\nthis test even if it renamed the parameter.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 018 (D.8, #196): the one thing the call site does pass is the\noperator-ruling context, which is `''` unless a ruling exists under the\n`:ro` /config mount -- so `loop_mod.CONFIG_DIR` is pointed at an empty\nscratch directory here to keep this pin independent of whatever the\nhost running the suite has mounted. The non-empty case (a wave-scoped\nruling reaching this exact call site after a replan) is covered by\ntests/test_operator_ruling.py::\ntest_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791956453364,"stop":1791956453364,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791956453365,"stop":1791956453365,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791956536969,"stop":1791956536969,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791956536969,"stop":1791956536973,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791956536974,"stop":1791956536978,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,